        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "r3xpt",
          "x": 1470,
          "y": 80,
          "name": "Note / The Model",
          "width": 490,
          "height": 440,
          "content": "SEARCH & ADD — HOW IT WORKS\n\nThere are two different searches here, and they are deliberately NOT siblings in a tab bar. They differ on every axis: scope, what a result IS, what tapping a row does, and whether the library grows or shrinks.\n\n1 · IN-LIBRARY SEARCH — magnifier in the top bar\nScoped to THIS saved view only. Searching inside \"All Books\" can never return a movie. It narrows what is already on screen.\n\n2 · ONLINE SEARCH — orange + FAB, bottom right\nQueries one external provider (Openlibrary, Hardcover, Google Books) for things you do not own yet. Its rows say \"Add\", not \"Open\". Always scoped to the view's media type, so the provider list is derived and never asked for.\n\nGlobal cross-type search is a SEPARATE surface that lives on the Home screen only (Navigation / Search FAB). It is intentionally not reachable from this screen."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "m9L1v",
          "x": 1470,
          "y": 1080,
          "name": "Note / In-Library Search & Filters",
          "width": 490,
          "height": 510,
          "content": "ROW 2 · IN-LIBRARY SEARCH\n\nTapping the magnifier collapses the top bar into an input + Cancel. The back chevron is hidden while searching.\n\n· The \"10 of 128\" slot becomes the live result count.\n\n· The filter button is HIDDEN during search. Filters configure the saved view itself; they do not apply to search results. Showing both would imply a composition that does not happen.\n\nZero matches is the state that matters. It offers the escape hatch into online search and carries the typed query across, so the user never retypes it.\n\nFILTER / VIEW SHEET\nThe grid/list/table switcher used to float over the posters at bottom-right. It moved in here, next to sort and filters, because it is a per-view preference you set once — not something worth permanent screen space on a screen whose whole point is the artwork. That is what freed bottom-right for the Add FAB."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "yY6Ps",
          "x": 1470,
          "y": 2080,
          "name": "Note / Online Search & Create",
          "width": 490,
          "height": 520,
          "content": "ROW 3 · ONLINE SEARCH & CREATE\n\nReached from the orange + FAB, or from the escape hatch in a failed in-library search.\n\n· ONE provider at a time, never aggregated. The chosen provider decides which record becomes your library entity and supplies its metadata from then on, so it is a deliberate provenance choice — not a filter. Chips stay pinned above the results; the last choice is remembered per media type.\n\n· Items you already own show \"In library\" instead of \"Add\", so a duplicate cannot be created.\n\nMANUAL CREATE is intentionally gated behind a failed online search — it is only offered from the empty state. Manual entries are the main source of duplicate and junk records, so the online lookup is kept as the path of least resistance.\n\nAn EMPTY SAVED VIEW gets an inline CTA rather than a lone FAB, and dims its search/filter controls since there is nothing yet to search or filter."
        }
      ]
    },
